CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "cff11fda-5f0d-450b-8113-6277664fb8e5",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T19:57:06Z",
  "ticket_id": "750c-6033-e04f-4682",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "SC1 \u2014 Verifier as load-bearing pre-commit gate. A new pre-commit hook (parity tier with existing test-gate / review-gate) reads the breadcrumb log and wrapper-written validation artifacts for the worktree where the commit is being made and refuses the commit when (a) any expected artifact is missing for a step that should have run under the active enforcement.strategy and SKIP_REVIEW state, or (b) the classifier flagged one or more REVIEW overlays without their corresponding findings artifacts. Test fixtures: synthetically removing a wrapper artifact triggers the block; synthetic missing overlay findings file (with classifier-flagged overlay) triggers the block. Regression tests reproduce the failure surfaces of bugs 94e8-9f91 (overlay flags ignored) and 7b41-3061 (empty breadcrumb log) and confirm both are mechanically prevented as a direct consequence of SC1's enforcement.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (pre-commit gate enforcement) that prevents invalid commits going forward, phrased as ongoing behavior despite the detailed implementation narrative"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC2 \u2014 Truncation-masking immunity. Validation commands (test, format, lint, classifier dispatch, reviewer dispatch) run through wrappers that capture full output into result artifacts. The verifier reads from the artifact, not from the agent's terminal stream. Test fixture: an agent invoking the wrapper with `2>&1 | tail -3` (or any other agent-side output filter) does not change what the verifier sees and does not allow a hidden lint/test failure to slip through.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system property where validation commands are immune to truncation, phrased as ongoing behavior the system maintains"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC3 \u2014 Per-commit interactive override path (release-blocking precondition for SC1). A hard-blocking gate is unsafe to deploy without a sane escape hatch for legitimate commits the gate gets wrong. Override is reachable only via explicit `dso commit-override --reason=\"<text>\"` invoked by the user (not the agent). Override applies to exactly one commit attempt and writes a durable audit record (in $ARTIFACTS_DIR and as a comment/trailer on the commit) listing the missing artifacts and the user's reason. Test fixture: a single override clears the next commit; a second attempt without re-authorization is blocked again. Cross-epic constraint: when dso-fbky autonomous mode is active, dso commit-override returns an error and the hook still blocks.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (interactive override mechanism with audit trails) that must exist and function correctly after this work, phrased as ongoing behavior"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC4 \u2014 Worktree-context safety in all three execution contexts. Verifier and wrappers behave correctly when commit runs in (a) the main repo, (b) a session worktree, (c) an isolated sub-agent worktree harvested back via the existing harvest-worktree.sh / record-test-status.sh --attest paths. Verifier reads artifacts only from the worktree where the commit is being made; sub-agent artifacts reach it only through the existing harvest path. A wrapper invoked from a CWD that does not match the worktree it would write to fails fast with a clear error rather than silently writing to a sibling worktree's artifacts dir. Test fixtures cover all three contexts plus the misconfigured-CWD failure mode.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior (correct worktree-context safety across execution contexts) that persists after implementation, though the lengthy description conflates behavior with test coverage requirements"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "SC5 \u2014 Conditional-step skip markers and zero false-positive baseline. Legitimately-skipped steps (e.g., enforcement.strategy=ci, SKIP_REVIEW=true, commands.test_changed unset) emit explicit `skipped:<reason>` artifacts that the verifier accepts. A passing run of validate.sh --ci and a clean DSO-self-commit on this epic demonstrate the verifier introduces zero false positives on existing valid commit paths \u2014 the gate fires only on actual non-compliance.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system capability where the verifier reliably emits skip markers and accepts them without false positives"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
}
